==> tests/test_e2e_stdin_detached.sh <==
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# B2 lint: tests/e2e.sh must detach stdin (`</dev/null`) from every
# interactive-by-default subprocess it spawns (QEMU `-nographic`, vsim under
# `timeout`). Without it, a backgrounded shell group (scripts/run_e2e.sh uses
# one) lets SIGTTOU stop the child when it calls tcsetattr on the inherited
# controlling tty. Diagnostic tell: empty log + rc=124 + /proc/$PID/status
# State `T`. See memory `feedback_qemu_timeout_sigttou`.
#
# This is a static lint: it greps the QEMU1 and vsim invocation blocks in
# tests/e2e.sh for the `</dev/null` redirect. Catches accidental removal of
# the SIGTTOU workaround without needing a real QEMU/vsim build.
==> tests/test_kernel_cycles.sh <==
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# tests/e2e.sh must print kernel_cycles -- the vsim mcycle delta over the
# measured region (vsim drain - QEMU1 drain, offset 624) -- for both
# trigger modes (marker, pc), so the `./andesim run --mode hybrid
# --trigger marker|pc` surface carries the cycle figure.
#
# Fixture: rt_c_v_matmul.elf (marked RVV GEMM). Marker mode uses the
# ROI marker HINTs in the source; PC mode resolves the boundaries
# from the binary itself (no planted _hybrid_*_pc labels).
#
# Manual TDD smoke test (runs real QEMU+vsim round-trips); not wired into
# scripts/run_e2e.sh.
==> tests/lib/roi.test.sh <==
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# RED->GREEN: resolve_pc maps an ROI boundary (a symbol name OR a 0x-hex
# address) to a bare hex address, resolving symbols against `nm` output.
# This is the primitive that lets pc mode point at ANY symbol/address
1:// rt_all_fprs.S
// Phase A (QEMU1):
//   Enable mstatus.FS, then f_i = 0xF0D0_0000_0000_0000 + i for i in 0..31,
//   moved in via fmv.d.x. The plugin drains f0..f31 into hybrid_state_v1.fpr[].
// Phase B (vsim): the FPR block-load restores f0..f31; the ROI is empty.
//   --verify compares the drained fpr[] against the QEMU oracle field by field
//   -- a wrong fld offset/order lands a value in the wrong f-reg and fails.
// Phase C (standalone only -- markers are NOPs): read each f-reg back via
//   fmv.x.d and compare; exit code = (first mismatching freg + 1), 0 on pass.
//
// fmv.d.x / fmv.x.d move the raw 64 bits with no canonicalization, so any bit
// pattern round-trips exactly (no NaN-boxing as with the .s single moves).

